# The sixteen talking sarcophagi of the Amber Temple (docs/regions/amber_temple.md §4.3; voices: docs/voice/amber_vestiges.md).
# Ring of amber (amber_temple_faceless_god): zantras, fekre, taar_haak, shami_amourae, yog, drizlash.
# Hall of vestiges (amber_temple_vault): khirad, norganas, savnok, seriach, sykane, tarakamedes, tenebrous, yrrga,
# zhudun, dahlver_nar. Each node: sealed / already gave its gift / heard before / first hearing, then a menu (want,
# offer, the lid inscription, personal hooks). The offer reaches `dark_gift <id>`: the player picks who accepts, or
# no one. Refusal options come first in each menu. Gifts: data/dark_gifts/.

~ sealed
Narrator: The amber is dark and cold. Whatever is inside is still there, but the wardens' seal holds, and for once it has nothing to say.
-> END

# ================================================================================================ The ring of amber

~ zantras
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_zantras
Narrator: The crowned figure no longer looks at the room. It looks only at whoever carries its gift, the way a proud parent watches a child on a stage.
vestige_zantras: Stand up straight. They're watching.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_zantras_heard
vestige_zantras: My audience returns. I knew you couldn't stay away. Nobody ever can.
-> zantras_menu
endif
set vestige_zantras_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: In the amber stands a gaunt figure crowned with something that might be gold and might be teeth. One hand is raised to bless a crowd that left a very long time ago. Its eyes follow whoever is talking.
vestige_zantras: At last. An audience. Do you know how long it has been since anyone looked at me? Come closer. You, at the front. You were made to be looked at, and nobody has noticed. I could fix that.
-> zantras_menu

~ zantras_menu
* What do you want with us? -> zantras_want
* What are you offering? -> zantras_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> zantras_lid | zantras_lid_fail
* [if guest:ireena] (It's looking at Ireena.) -> zantras_ireena
* [name:ratatoille] [if not flag.ratatoille_zantras_refused and not gift:gift_of_zantras] (Ratatoille has gone very still, listening.) -> companions/table:zantras
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ zantras_want
vestige_zantras: A king is only a mirror the crowd stands in front of. Mine broke a long time ago. I need a new one, with a pulse.
interject tag:proud: I won't pretend that isn't tempting. I will pretend it's beneath me, which is different.
-> zantras_menu

~ zantras_offer
vestige_zantras: When you walk into a room, it will turn. When you speak, people will lean in. Kings will stammer beside you, and you will never again be the one nobody remembers.
* And the price? -> zantras_price
* No. -> zantras_refuse
* I accept. -> zantras_accept

~ zantras_price
vestige_zantras: Hardly worth the mention. You'll need them to keep looking. Every hour. And people who aren't looking at you will stop being interesting. What use were they anyway?
* No. -> zantras_refuse
* I accept. -> zantras_accept

~ zantras_lid
Narrator: The wardens' inscription, in our own plain words: "Zantras, who crowned beggars. Every king it made was pulled apart by the crowd that loved him. Do not look at it for long."
-> zantras_menu

~ zantras_lid_fail
Narrator: Frost has softened the lid's letters to dimples. You make out the name, and the word "crowd", and nothing kind.
-> zantras_menu

~ zantras_ireena
vestige_zantras: And you, my dear. You already have it, don't you? Everyone looks at you. Strangers, wolves, lords on hills. Do you hate it yet?
interject guest:ireena: Every day of my life.
vestige_zantras: Then give it to one of them. Gifts can be passed along, you know, if you're generous.
-> zantras_menu

~ zantras_accept
dark_gift gift_of_zantras
if gift:gift_of_zantras
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name} straightens without meaning to. In the dim hall, the light finds them first now, and stays.
vestige_zantras: There. Now they'll see you. Make sure they never stop.
else
vestige_zantras: No one? A crowd of nobodies. How fitting. Off you go, then. Nobody will notice.
endif
-> END

~ zantras_refuse
vestige_zantras: Then go back to being furniture. I'll be here when you tire of it.
-> END

~ fekre
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_fekre
Narrator: The bubbles in the clouded amber drift toward whoever carries Fekre's gift, like children crowding a window.
vestige_fekre: There's my darling. Keeping warm? Keeping everyone warm? Good.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_fekre_heard
vestige_fekre: Back again, my poor dears. Still coughing? You'll be coughing by spring.
-> fekre_menu
endif
set vestige_fekre_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: A swollen, motherly shape fills the clouded amber, ringed with tiny bubbles like a rash. The air near the lid tastes of sickrooms and boiled linen.
vestige_fekre: Oh, my poor lambs, you've come so far in the cold. Your lips are cracked. That one's cough will settle in the chest. Come to mother. Mother takes care of fevers.
-> fekre_menu

~ fekre_menu
* What do you want with us? -> fekre_want
* What are you offering? -> fekre_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> fekre_lid | fekre_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ fekre_want
vestige_fekre: Children, sweetling. Mine are everywhere: every fever, every flux, every rash in every village. I would so like one that walks.
interject class:cleric: I have nursed plague wards. You are not a mother. You're what mothers pray against.
vestige_fekre: And yet they all call for mother, at the end. Ask any child with a fever.
-> fekre_menu

~ fekre_offer
vestige_fekre: No poison will ever touch you again, my lamb. No plague, no rot in a wound. And when someone hurts you, you can breathe it back on them and watch them wilt.
* And the price? -> fekre_price
* No. -> fekre_refuse
* I accept. -> fekre_accept

~ fekre_price
vestige_fekre: Mother's children like to visit. They'll stay with you, and with whoever sits near you. And a body that holds so much sickness is slow to mend. Healing will do half its work on you. Only half, dear.
* No. -> fekre_refuse
* I accept. -> fekre_accept

~ fekre_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Fekre, the mother of fevers. She emptied a city by loving it. Wash your hands after."
-> fekre_menu

~ fekre_lid_fail
Narrator: The lid is crusted with something that isn't frost. You decide not to scrape it off to read underneath.
-> fekre_menu

~ fekre_accept
dark_gift gift_of_fekre
if gift:gift_of_fekre
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name} coughs once, hard, and then breathes easier than they have in weeks. Somewhere behind you, someone sneezes.
vestige_fekre: There, my darling. Now you'll never be lonely again.
else
vestige_fekre: Nobody? Ungrateful children. Never mind. You'll come back when you're feverish. Everyone does.
endif
-> END

~ fekre_refuse
vestige_fekre: Off you go, then. Wrap up warm. Not that it helps.
-> END

~ taar_haak
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_taar_haak
Narrator: All five mouths in the amber seem to have turned toward whoever carries the gift, and all five are grinning.
vestige_taar_haak: FOUND ANYTHING? BROKEN IT? GOOD. MORE.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_taar_haak_heard
vestige_taar_haak: Back. Still soft. One of us said you'd be back. One of us said you'd run. Three of us bet on blood.
-> taar_haak_menu
endif
set vestige_taar_haak_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: Five heads on five thick necks crowd the amber, every mouth open. You can't tell whether they are roaring or laughing. The inside of the lid is scored with claw marks.
vestige_taar_haak: SMALL. SOFT. WHICH OF YOU HITS HARDEST? That one. No, that one. We'll decide later. Come closer, little fist.
-> taar_haak_menu

~ taar_haak_menu
* What do you want with us? -> taar_haak_want
* What are you offering? -> taar_haak_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> taar_haak_lid | taar_haak_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ taar_haak_want
vestige_taar_haak: War. Any war. Yours will do. One of us is hungry, one of us is angry, and the other three are worse.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Sir Pellam went to three wars. He said they all end the same way: somebody digging.
vestige_taar_haak: Was it a good ending? Tell us about the ending.
-> taar_haak_menu

~ taar_haak_offer
vestige_taar_haak: Arms that break doors. A back that carries the dead home. You'll kill the things that laugh at you now, and you'll enjoy it. That's the best part.
* And the price? -> taar_haak_price
* No. -> taar_haak_refuse
* I accept. -> taar_haak_accept

~ taar_haak_price
vestige_taar_haak: We come too. All five, in your skull. Thinking is slow. Arguing is slower. You'll stop doing both. And once you start, you won't stop. Stopping is for cowards. We hate cowards.
* No. -> taar_haak_refuse
* I accept. -> taar_haak_accept

~ taar_haak_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Great Taar Haak, the five-throated war. The armies that worshipped it did not survive it."
-> taar_haak_menu

~ taar_haak_lid_fail
Narrator: Most of the inscription has been clawed away, from the inside. That tells you more than the words would have.
-> taar_haak_menu

~ taar_haak_accept
dark_gift gift_of_taar_haak
if gift:gift_of_taar_haak
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name}'s shoulders crack like logs on a fire. Their hands open and close, open and close, as if looking for a throat.
vestige_taar_haak: GO. FIND SOMETHING. BREAK IT. We'll watch from the inside.
else
vestige_taar_haak: COWARDS. ALL OF YOU. Two of us are disappointed. Three of us expected it.
endif
-> END

~ taar_haak_refuse
vestige_taar_haak: Run, then, soft things. Something bigger will catch you. We'd have liked to watch.
-> END

~ shami_amourae
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_shami_amourae
Narrator: The figure in the clear amber has turned over in its sleep, toward whoever carries its gift, and its smile has grown a little wider.
vestige_shami_amourae: There you are. Have you been enjoying yourself? Don't answer. I can tell.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_shami_amourae_heard
vestige_shami_amourae: You came back. Of course you did. Sit with me a while.
-> shami_amourae_menu
endif
set vestige_shami_amourae_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: A lovely figure lies curled in the clear amber as if asleep in a warm bed, one hand cupped as though holding out something sweet. When you look closer, the smile has a few too many teeth.
vestige_shami_amourae: Mm. You're cold. You're always cold here, aren't you? Nobody in this valley has touched you kindly in weeks. Come and sit by me. Just for a little while.
-> shami_amourae_menu

~ shami_amourae_menu
* What do you want with us? -> shami_amourae_want
* What are you offering? -> shami_amourae_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> shami_amourae_lid | shami_amourae_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ shami_amourae_want
vestige_shami_amourae: To be wanted, darling. Isn't that what everyone wants? I'm only more honest about it than you.
-> shami_amourae_menu

~ shami_amourae_offer
vestige_shami_amourae: Anyone you smile at will want to say yes, even the ones with claws. Especially them. And everything sweet will be sweeter: every cup, every kiss, every quiet hour.
* And the price? -> shami_amourae_price
* No. -> shami_amourae_refuse
* I accept. -> shami_amourae_accept

~ shami_amourae_price
vestige_shami_amourae: Only that you'll be as easy to persuade as you make everyone else. And you won't want to refuse a pleasure ever again. Why would you? I've never understood people who refuse.
interject tag:pious: That's not a price. That's a leash with ribbons on it.
* No. -> shami_amourae_refuse
* I accept. -> shami_amourae_accept

~ shami_amourae_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Shami-Amourae, the honeyed hand. Its lovers died smiling. All of them."
-> shami_amourae_menu

~ shami_amourae_lid_fail
Narrator: Someone has kissed the lid so often that the inscription has worn smooth. The prints of lips are still in the frost.
-> shami_amourae_menu

~ shami_amourae_accept
dark_gift gift_of_shami_amourae
if gift:gift_of_shami_amourae
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name} sighs like someone sinking into a hot bath, and doesn't notice the sound they've made.
vestige_shami_amourae: There. Isn't that better? Don't thank me. Just come back.
else
vestige_shami_amourae: Nobody? Not even a little? You'll lie awake wondering. I'll know.
endif
-> END

~ shami_amourae_refuse
vestige_shami_amourae: Shy. That's sweet too. I'll be here, darling. I'm always here.
-> END

~ yog
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_yog
Narrator: The hulk in the amber hasn't moved. It never moves. But the floor under your boots hums, once, like a pleased cat.
vestige_yog: Good. Endure.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_yog_heard
vestige_yog: ...Soft. Still.
-> yog_menu
endif
set vestige_yog_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: A squat, horned hulk like a boulder that grew limbs. Its hide is cracked like a dry riverbed. When it speaks, the voice comes up through the floor into the soles of your feet.
vestige_yog: Soft. You are... soft. Everything cuts you. That is... sad.
-> yog_menu

~ yog_menu
* What do you want with us? -> yog_want
* What are you offering? -> yog_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> yog_lid | yog_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ yog_want
vestige_yog: Want is soft. I... endure.
interject name:thistle: Grandda says rocks endure too. Never met anybody who wanted to be a rock.
-> yog_menu

~ yog_offer
vestige_yog: Skin like mine. Blades break. Teeth break. You... stay.
* And the price? -> yog_price
* No. -> yog_refuse
* I accept. -> yog_accept

~ yog_price
vestige_yog: Stone does not hurry. Stone does not... feel. You will be slow. You will not feel the sun. Or a hand. Does it matter? Hands are soft.
* No. -> yog_refuse
* I accept. -> yog_accept

~ yog_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Yog, the unbroken. It outlasted everyone who worshipped it. That was the whole of its gift, and the whole of its price."
-> yog_menu

~ yog_lid_fail
Narrator: The letters are cut so shallow that the stone seems to have healed over them. Of course it has.
-> yog_menu

~ yog_accept
dark_gift gift_of_yog
if gift:gift_of_yog
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name}'s skin greys and tightens with the creak of old leather. When a friend touches their arm, {name} doesn't turn around.
vestige_yog: Good. Now... endure.
else
vestige_yog: ...Soft.
endif
-> END

~ yog_refuse
vestige_yog: Then break. I will be here after.
-> END

~ drizlash
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_drizlash
Narrator: Every black eye in the amber turns at once to whoever carries the gift. Four small black eyes along their hairline turn back.
vestige_drizlash: Seeing well? Seeing everything? Yes, yes, yes.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_drizlash_heard
vestige_drizlash: Back, back, back. I watched you go. I watched you come. I watch.
-> drizlash_menu
endif
set vestige_drizlash_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: Something spidery is folded in on itself in the amber, legs over legs, crowned with a ring of small black eyes. Every eye turns to you at once.
vestige_drizlash: There you are, there you are. I saw you on the stair. I saw you on the ledge. I see the knife in the small one's boot. I see everything, and I could let you see it too.
-> drizlash_menu

~ drizlash_menu
* What do you want with us? -> drizlash_want
* What are you offering? -> drizlash_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> drizlash_lid | drizlash_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ drizlash_want
vestige_drizlash: Walls. Webs. The dark corners nobody looks in. Room to spin, room to spin.
interject class:rogue: Walking up walls is a terrible idea, and I'd use it every night of my life.
-> drizlash_menu

~ drizlash_offer
vestige_drizlash: Walk the walls. Walk the ceiling. See in the black as if it were noon. And spin, spin, spin: a web from your own palms to hold what you catch.
* And the price? -> drizlash_price
* No. -> drizlash_refuse
* I accept. -> drizlash_accept

~ drizlash_price
vestige_drizlash: My eyes. You'll wear four of mine. They don't close, and they don't like the sun. And people stare. People always stare at eyes.
* No. -> drizlash_refuse
* I accept. -> drizlash_accept

~ drizlash_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Drizlash, who spins between the walls. Its priests lived in the dark, and were glad of it, and never came out."
-> drizlash_menu

~ drizlash_lid_fail
Narrator: Webs as fine as breath cover the lid. Under them the letters are there, but the webs move when you try to read.
-> drizlash_menu

~ drizlash_accept
dark_gift gift_of_drizlash
if gift:gift_of_drizlash
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name} blinks, and four small black eyes along their hairline blink a moment later.
vestige_drizlash: Now you see. Now you see. Now you see.
else
vestige_drizlash: No one, no one. I'll watch you go, then. I'll watch you all the way down.
endif
-> END

~ drizlash_refuse
vestige_drizlash: Go, go. I'll see you. I always see you.
-> END

# ================================================================================================ The hall of vestiges

~ khirad
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_khirad
Narrator: The thin figure in the amber has stopped reading its missing sky. It looks at whoever carries its gift with something like pity.
vestige_khirad: You've seen how it ends by now. I'm sorry. I'm always sorry, after.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_khirad_heard
vestige_khirad: You came back. I read that you would. You were taller in the reading.
-> khirad_menu
endif
set vestige_khirad_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: A thin figure in the amber has its face tipped up, eyes wide, lips moving, as if reading a sky that isn't there. The amber over its eyes is scratched, from the inside.
vestige_khirad: You came. I read that you would, eleven centuries ago, in a star that has since gone out. Sit. Let me tell you how this ends.
-> khirad_menu

~ khirad_menu
* What do you want with us? -> khirad_want
* What are you offering? -> khirad_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> khirad_lid | khirad_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ khirad_want
vestige_khirad: Someone to read to. The stars are dull company. They only know one story, and they insist on telling it to the end.
-> khirad_menu

~ khirad_offer
vestige_khirad: Sight. You'll know the next breath before it's drawn, the next blade before it falls. And once a day you may look anywhere at all, as if you stood there.
* And the price? -> khirad_price
* No. -> khirad_refuse
* I accept. -> khirad_accept

~ khirad_price
vestige_khirad: You'll see every way a moment can end. Most of them end badly. You won't sleep well. Nobody who reads the stars sleeps well. Ask any of us. Ask me.
* No. -> khirad_refuse
* I accept. -> khirad_accept

~ khirad_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Khirad, who reads the stars backward. Everything it foretold came true. Its readers wished it hadn't."
-> khirad_menu

~ khirad_lid_fail
Narrator: The inscription has been scratched over with tiny star charts. Someone sat here a long time, copying what the vestige told them.
-> khirad_menu

~ khirad_accept
dark_gift gift_of_khirad
if gift:gift_of_khirad
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name}'s pupils widen and stay wide. For a heartbeat they look at each of you as though remembering your funerals.
vestige_khirad: There. Now you know. I'm sorry.
else
vestige_khirad: No one. I read that too. I always hope I've misread.
endif
-> END

~ khirad_refuse
vestige_khirad: As you like. It ends the same way either way. Only the knowing changes.
-> END

~ norganas
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_norganas
Narrator: The blurred shape in the milky amber seems a little sharper than before, as if it had been fed.
vestige_norganas: Hello. Have we... no. You wouldn't remember.
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_norganas_heard
vestige_norganas: Hello. Have we met? ...No, I don't suppose you'd know either.
-> norganas_menu
endif
set vestige_norganas_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: Something in the milky amber is blurred, as though the sculptor kept rubbing it out and starting again. The longer you look, the less you could say what shape it is.
vestige_norganas: Hello. Have we... no. No, we haven't. Nobody remembers meeting me. That is rather the point of me.
-> norganas_menu

~ norganas_menu
* What do you want with us? -> norganas_want
* What are you offering? -> norganas_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> norganas_lid | norganas_lid_fail
* [if flag.exethanter_met] Exethanter, the warden upstairs. Did he bargain with you? -> norganas_warden
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ norganas_want
vestige_norganas: Quiet. Every name, every war, every song, rubbed out. A clean page. Doesn't that sound restful? You look so tired.
-> norganas_menu

~ norganas_offer
vestige_norganas: Point. That's all it takes. Point at anything that lives, and I'll rub it out from the inside. Once a day. You'll be the most frightening thing in any room you walk into.
* And the price? -> norganas_price
* No. -> norganas_refuse
* I accept. -> norganas_accept

~ norganas_price
vestige_norganas: I eat what you know. A little now. A little more each time you use me. You won't miss it. You won't remember what it was.
interject class:wizard: Everything I am is what I know. You're offering me a sword and asking for the hand.
* No. -> norganas_refuse
* I accept. -> norganas_accept

~ norganas_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Norganas, the eraser. It has been forgotten twice already." Below, in a newer, shakier hand: "Warden, if you can't remember why you carved this: you asked it to take the voices. It took you."
-> norganas_menu

~ norganas_lid_fail
Narrator: The inscription is there, and you read it, and a moment later you can't recall a word of it. You read it again. The same thing happens.
-> norganas_menu

~ norganas_warden
set exethanter_bargain_known
vestige_norganas: Who? ...Oh. The careful one. He asked me to take the whispering out of his head. I took the whispering. Then I kept taking. He was delicious. He still is, a little at a time.
-> norganas_menu

~ norganas_accept
