Narrator: A hooded figure sits with its mouth sewn shut and its hands folded over a small closed box. The voice, when it comes, comes from inside the box.
vestige_savnok: ...You have secrets. Everyone does. Shall I keep them for you?
-> savnok_menu

~ savnok_menu
* What do you want with us? -> savnok_want
* What are you offering? -> savnok_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> savnok_lid | savnok_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ savnok_want
vestige_savnok: ...Keys. Locks. Things unsaid.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Keys, locks and things unsaid. Has somebody been going through my pack?
-> savnok_menu

~ savnok_offer
vestige_savnok: A locked mind. No charm, no whisper, no lord's sweet voice will ever open it. The one on the hill opens minds like letters. Not yours. And lies will come as easily as breathing.
* And the price? -> savnok_price
* No. -> savnok_refuse
* I accept. -> savnok_accept

~ savnok_price
vestige_savnok: ...A locked box doesn't open from the inside either. You won't speak a true word of yourself again. You won't hear much. And no one will quite believe you, even when you mean it.
* No. -> savnok_refuse
* I accept. -> savnok_accept

~ savnok_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Savnok, the locked mouth. Its keepers never told us what it wanted. They couldn't."
-> savnok_menu

~ savnok_lid_fail
