Narrator: A lean figure in the amber holds a fistful of chains, and every chain ends in the snarling head of a hound. The amber around the hounds is clouded, like smoke.
vestige_seriach: Hear them? They've had your scent since the stair. Good noses, my dogs. They never lose a quarry. Want one of them to run with you?
-> seriach_menu

~ seriach_menu
* What do you want with us? -> seriach_want
* What are you offering? -> seriach_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> seriach_lid | seriach_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ seriach_want
vestige_seriach: The hunt. Always the hunt. Whose hunt hardly matters.
interject class:ranger: Hounds that never lose a scent. In my trade that's not a gift. It's a curse on a leash.
-> seriach_menu

~ seriach_offer
vestige_seriach: Fire in the blood. Your blows will burn like my hounds' teeth, and flame will slide off you like rain off a dog's back.
* And the price? -> seriach_price
* No. -> seriach_refuse
* I accept. -> seriach_accept

~ seriach_price
vestige_seriach: My hounds will follow you. Always. Every beast you meet will smell them and bolt, or bite. And fire hates the cold, hunter. Look where you're standing.
* No. -> seriach_refuse
* I accept. -> seriach_accept

~ seriach_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Seriach, master of the burning hounds. Its hunts did not end when the quarry died."
-> seriach_menu

~ seriach_lid_fail
