if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: The skull and coiled spine of a dragon fill the amber, packed so tight the bones have cracked. The amber is the dark red of old blood, and it is cold even to look at.
vestige_tarakamedes: Little warm things. You stand on the graves of my servants and don't even know it. Kneel or don't. The grave is patient either way.
-> tarakamedes_menu

~ tarakamedes_menu
* What do you want with us? -> tarakamedes_want
* What are you offering? -> tarakamedes_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> tarakamedes_lid | tarakamedes_lid_fail
* [if flag.doru_cure_promised] Is there a cure for a vampire's bite? -> tarakamedes_doru
* [if guest:kasimir_velikov and not flag.kasimir_bargain and not flag.patrina_fate and not flag.patrina_destroyed] (Kasimir steps up to the amber.) -> tarakamedes_kasimir
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ tarakamedes_want
vestige_tarakamedes: Every life ends in my mouth. I would like, once, to be thanked for it.
-> tarakamedes_menu

~ tarakamedes_offer
vestige_tarakamedes: The dead will hear you. They'll rise when you call and answer when you ask. And the grave's cold won't bite you any more. It knows you'll be along.
* And the price? -> tarakamedes_price
* No. -> tarakamedes_refuse
* I accept. -> tarakamedes_accept

~ tarakamedes_price
vestige_tarakamedes: You'll owe me, only at the end. When you fall, I'll be waiting just under the floor of the world, and I'll pull. Gently. Without stopping.
* No. -> tarakamedes_refuse
* I accept. -> tarakamedes_accept

~ tarakamedes_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Tarakamedes, the dragon in the grave. Its faithful went down into the earth to serve it. None came back up."
-> tarakamedes_menu

~ tarakamedes_lid_fail
Narrator: The lid is so cold that your breath freezes on it, and the frost fills the letters before you can read them.
-> tarakamedes_menu

~ tarakamedes_doru
vestige_tarakamedes: For the priest's boy, in the village? There is no cure. There is only me. Bring him here and I'll make him something that doesn't need blood. You wouldn't like what it needs instead.
interject class:cleric: Then we keep looking. Or we keep our word another way.
-> tarakamedes_menu

~ tarakamedes_kasimir
Kasimir: My sister. Patrina. Her bones lie under the castle and her voice is in this temple. Can you put them together again?
vestige_tarakamedes: Bones, voice, breath. The work of a moment. The price is yours, elf: every year you have left, but one. One year with her. Then you come down to me.
Kasimir: One year. I have wasted three hundred.
* Let him choose. -> tarakamedes_kasimir_yes
* [Persuasion DC 15] She went to the castle the first time, Kasimir. She'll go again. -> tarakamedes_kasimir_no | tarakamedes_kasimir_yes
* [if flag.patrina_met] You heard her. She doesn't want to be bought back. -> tarakamedes_kasimir_no

~ tarakamedes_kasimir_yes
set kasimir_bargain = "made"
set patrina_fate = "restored"
quest patrinas_wail restored
Kasimir: Then I will be brave once, and late. Take it.
Narrator: The red amber flares. Kasimir staggers, and when he straightens, his white hair has gone the grey of old ash and there are lines at his eyes that weren't there a breath ago.
Narrator: Far above, in the hall of echoes, the wailing stops. Later you'll find footprints in the frost: bare, narrow, walking out through the doors and down the mountain, toward the castle.
Kasimir [sad]: She didn't wait. Of course she didn't wait. She never once waited for me.
approve wren_featherfoot -3 liriel_dawnsong -2 kip_smudgewick -2: Kasimir bought Patrina back from the amber, and you let him
-> END

~ tarakamedes_kasimir_no
set kasimir_bargain = "refused"
Kasimir: ...Yes. You're right. I know you're right. It is a terrible thing, to be talked out of the only brave thing I nearly did.
vestige_tarakamedes: Patience, elf. Everyone comes down to me in the end. I don't need to bargain for you.
approve wren_featherfoot +4 liriel_dawnsong +2 kip_smudgewick +1: You talked Kasimir out of buying his sister back
-> END

~ tarakamedes_accept
dark_gift gift_of_tarakamedes
if gift:gift_of_tarakamedes
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name}'s breath fogs, though nobody else's does. Under the floor, something very large shifts, and settles.
vestige_tarakamedes: I'll see you again. Everyone does.
else
vestige_tarakamedes: No one. It makes no difference. I'll have you all eventually, without the paperwork.
endif
-> END

~ tarakamedes_refuse
vestige_tarakamedes: Walk away, then. Every road you take goes downhill to me.
-> END

