vestige_tenebrous: The last candle out. The last star. And then, at last, rest.
interject class:cleric: You want the last light out. I carry one. We have nothing to discuss.
-> tenebrous_menu

~ tenebrous_offer
vestige_tenebrous: The dark will be your house. You'll see in it and walk in it unseen, and call it down over any room like a curtain.
* And the price? -> tenebrous_price
* No. -> tenebrous_refuse
* I accept. -> tenebrous_accept

~ tenebrous_price
vestige_tenebrous: Light will be your enemy. Sunlight, holy fire, the bright things priests throw. They'll cut you like a thief caught in a doorway.
* No. -> tenebrous_refuse
* I accept. -> tenebrous_accept

~ tenebrous_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Tenebrous, the last shadow. When the stars go out, this is what remains. We put it here to make sure it waits its turn."
-> tenebrous_menu

~ tenebrous_lid_fail
Narrator: Your light won't settle on the lid. It slides off the letters as if the stone were wet with ink.
-> tenebrous_menu

~ tenebrous_accept
