Narrator: One great lidless eye fills the amber, its pupil as wide as a cartwheel. It isn't looking at you. It's looking at something just behind you, and it has been for a very long time.
vestige_yrrga: Oh. You can't see it. You can't see any of it. The masks, the borrowed skins, the thing standing just behind the one you love. How do you live like that?
-> yrrga_menu

~ yrrga_menu
* What do you want with us? -> yrrga_want
* What are you offering? -> yrrga_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> yrrga_lid | yrrga_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ yrrga_want
