-> yrrga_menu

~ yrrga_offer
vestige_yrrga: Your eyes, made true. Illusions, disguises, invisible things, borrowed faces: none of them will fool you up close. Not even his. You'd see the lord on the hill as he is.
* And the price? -> yrrga_price
* No. -> yrrga_refuse
* I accept. -> yrrga_accept

~ yrrga_price
vestige_yrrga: You'll see what's really there. All of it, all the time. Courage is mostly not seeing. You'll lose it.
* No. -> yrrga_refuse
* I accept. -> yrrga_accept

~ yrrga_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Yrrga, the eye that opened outside. Its priests put out their own eyes. It was a mercy, and they knew it."
-> yrrga_menu

~ yrrga_lid_fail
Narrator: You bend to read the lid, and feel the eye on the back of your neck the whole time. You read nothing. You straighten up quickly.
-> yrrga_menu

~ yrrga_accept
dark_gift gift_of_yrrga
if gift:gift_of_yrrga
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name}'s eyes water, then clear. They look at each of you in turn, for too long, and say nothing about what they see.
