endif
endif
Narrator: A dull grey sphere hangs in black amber, giving off a cold light that lights nothing around it. Looking at it is like looking at the moon through ice.
vestige_zhudun: I was a sun once. Worlds turned around me. Now I am a cinder in a jar. Come closer. I still have a little light.
-> zhudun_menu

~ zhudun_menu
* What do you want with us? -> zhudun_want
* What are you offering? -> zhudun_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> zhudun_lid | zhudun_lid_fail
* [name:liriel_dawnsong] You're not the dawn. -> zhudun_liriel
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ zhudun_want
vestige_zhudun: To shine again. On someone. Anyone.
-> zhudun_menu

~ zhudun_offer
vestige_zhudun: My light, under your skin: cold, and untouched by the holy fire your priests throw. And once a day, a door into the black between the stars, opened in your enemies' midst.
* And the price? -> zhudun_price
* No. -> zhudun_refuse
* I accept. -> zhudun_accept

~ zhudun_price
vestige_zhudun: A dead star is cold all the way through. You'll be frailer, slow to warm, and fire will find you like dry kindling. And you'll glow in the dark, always, just a little. Grey.
* No. -> zhudun_refuse
* I accept. -> zhudun_accept

~ zhudun_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Zhudun, the dead star. It burned out. It did not go out."
-> zhudun_menu

~ zhudun_lid_fail
Narrator: The grey light makes every letter look the same. You give up before your eyes start to ache.
-> zhudun_menu

~ zhudun_liriel
vestige_zhudun: No. But you haven't felt your dawn since you came through the mist, have you, little priestess? Not once. I can feel how cold you are. Let me be your light. I'm right here, and he isn't.
Player: He isn't here. I know. That is what faith is for. You need none; you are right here. That is how I know you are not him.
inspire name:liriel_dawnsong: told a vestige to its face that it was not the dawn
approve liriel_dawnsong +3: You let me tell the false dawn what it was
-> zhudun_menu

~ zhudun_accept
dark_gift gift_of_zhudun
if gift:gift_of_zhudun
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name} glows, faintly, grey, like a candle seen through frosted glass. It doesn't warm the room at all.
vestige_zhudun: There. Shine for me.
else
vestige_zhudun: No one. Then stay in your little dark. I'll go on shining at nobody. I'm used to it.
endif
-> END

~ zhudun_refuse
vestige_zhudun: Go and look for your dawn, then. Tell me if you find it.
-> END

~ dahlver_nar
if flag.amber_temple_sealed
-> sealed
endif
if gift:gift_of_dahlver_nar
Narrator: Every tooth in the great jaw seems to be smiling at whoever carries the gift. They have a great deal in common now.
vestige_dahlver_nar: Hello, hello. How are our teeth? Chewing well?
-> END
endif
if flag.vestige_dahlver_nar_heard
vestige_dahlver_nar: Back again, back again. Say something. Anything. We do love a new voice.
-> dahlver_nar_menu
endif
set vestige_dahlver_nar_heard
if not flag.amber_voices_begun
set amber_voices_begun
if not quest.the_amber_temple >= voices_heard
quest the_amber_temple voices_heard
endif
endif
Narrator: A huge jaw fills the amber, lined with row on row of teeth: a man's, a horse's, a child's milk teeth, a wolf's fang. No two come from the same mouth.
vestige_dahlver_nar: Hello. Hello. Hello. Don't mind us; we're all in here, every mouth we ever borrowed. Say something, would you? We'd love a new voice.
-> dahlver_nar_menu

~ dahlver_nar_menu
* What do you want with us? -> dahlver_nar_want
* What are you offering? -> dahlver_nar_offer
* [History DC 13] Read the wardens' inscription on the lid. -> dahlver_nar_lid | dahlver_nar_lid_fail
* (Step away from the amber.) -> END

~ dahlver_nar_want
vestige_dahlver_nar: Mouths. Teeth. Voices. We collect, you see. We're collectors.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Never sell to a collector, Mum says. They pay beautifully, and then one day you're in the cabinet.
-> dahlver_nar_menu

~ dahlver_nar_offer
vestige_dahlver_nar: You'll be so hard to kill. Cut you, burn you, drop you off a mountain, and something in you keeps chewing on, and on, and gets back up.
* And the price? -> dahlver_nar_price
* No. -> dahlver_nar_refuse
* I accept. -> dahlver_nar_accept

~ dahlver_nar_price
vestige_dahlver_nar: Your teeth. All of them, overnight, for some of ours. People won't like your smile. And when you're tired you'll talk in other people's voices. They'll be fine. Mostly.
* No. -> dahlver_nar_refuse
* I accept. -> dahlver_nar_accept

~ dahlver_nar_lid
Narrator: The inscription, in plain words: "Dahlver-Nar, the mouth of borrowed teeth. It cannot make anything. It only keeps."
-> dahlver_nar_menu

~ dahlver_nar_lid_fail
Narrator: Someone has pressed teeth into the soft stone of the lid, in rows, over the words. You stop trying to read it.
-> dahlver_nar_menu

~ dahlver_nar_accept
dark_gift gift_of_dahlver_nar
if gift:gift_of_dahlver_nar
set dark_gifts_taken += 1
approve liriel_dawnsong -5 kip_smudgewick -5 godrick_pendlebrook -4 wren_featherfoot -3 thistle -2 ratatoille -2: You let one of us take a Dark Gift from the amber
Narrator: {name} winces and puts a hand to their jaw. When they take it away and smile, nobody smiles back.
vestige_dahlver_nar: Lovely. Lovely. Say something. Ah, that's a good one.
else
vestige_dahlver_nar: Nobody? Pity. Pity. Pity. We'll remember your voices anyway.
endif
-> END

~ dahlver_nar_refuse
vestige_dahlver_nar: Goodbye, goodbye, goodbye. We'll practise your voices while you're away.
-> END
